WEBVTT

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:02.780
Yume-chan!

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:04.770
Let's go home!

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.480
Sorry.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.530
I was hoping to stop by the study hall today.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:12.030
Aw, really?

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.090
No sulking, Aki.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:16.490
You'll make her feel bad.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.400
And midterms start tomorrow, after all.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.410
Maybe <i>we</i> should be the ones feeling bad.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.870
I-I wouldn't say that...

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.660
You took the top score 
on the entrance exam, right?

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.420
I guess the defending champion
 has to pull out all the stops.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.260
Don't you, Irido-san?

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.260
Y-Yes...

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.400
<b>My Stepmom's 
Daughter Is 
My Ex</b>

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:11.560
<b>The Former Couple Goes Head-to-Head</b>

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:11.560
<b>"Do You Think I'm Stupid?!"</b>

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.730
<b>May</b>

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.730
Midterms

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:10.620
<i>Top score on the entrance exam.</i>

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.130
<i>A gifted student at the top of my year.</i>

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.570
Midterms

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:16.380
<i>This is where I belong.</i>

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:21.960
<i>It was my second year of middle school. 
We'd just taken our first midterms.</i>

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:24.440
<i>For the first time ever,</i>

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.790
<i>I was bested on a math test, 
despite it being one of my strengths...</i>

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:31.690
<i>by a boy in my class named Irido Mizuto.</i>

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.390
<i>I was devastated.</i>

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.790
<i>So when it came time for finals,</i>

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:42.120
<i>I sacrificed sleep to study 
more than ever before.</i>

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.180
<i>All in an effort to beat Irido Mizuto.</i>

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:50.500
<i>Fortunately, I was able to reclaim 
my spot at the top of the class.</i>

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:52.800
<i>However, when I looked at him,</i>

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.440
<i>he seemed indifferent to the 
way the teacher sang my praises.</i>

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:00.540
<i>He merely sat there, 
staring blankly out the window.</i>

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.210
<i>I felt hollow.</i>

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:06.680
<i>Like I'd conjured up a rivalry out of thin air.</i>

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:09.580
<i>And yet...</i>

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.210
Do you like mystery novels?

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.470
I-I do...

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:19.220
Now I get it. No wonder you 
get such good grades in math.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:22.300
<i>Our rivalry wasn't all in my head.</i>

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:26.010
<i>He'd just been pretending 
to look the other way,</i>

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:28.410
<i>when, in reality, 
he was watching me all along.</i>

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:35.400
<i>And with that, for the first
 time in my life, I fell in love.</i>

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:54.580
Are you sure you've done enough studying?

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.590
Yeah, I think I'm ready.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:03:59.590
Are you?

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:04.180
You act as though you're 
taking a far easier test than I am.

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:07.100
This is why I always beat you.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:07.430
<b>Our Last Crusade or the Rise of a New World

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:12.700
I wonder how good the seat 
at the top of the class feels.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:16.110
I'm afraid that seat is in 
my name at the moment.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:20.610
Then I'll just have to
 reserve it for next time.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:22.460
I see.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:25.410
So you plan on getting 
in my way again, do you?

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.450
I say go for it.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:29.740
Your chances are slim at best.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.920
Irido

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:42.980
You seem awfully tired.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:45.640
That's none of your concern.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:49.820
Is getting the top score 
really so important to you?

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:50.890
Of course it is.

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:53.050
Getting the top score
 on the entrance exam.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.450
Staying at the top of my year.

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:58.120
These are the reasons my 
life is the way it is now.

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:00.380
You wouldn't understand.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:02.330
You're too busy pretending.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:05.750
Living like you don't care about 
anything or anyone around you.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:08.280
A boy playing the lone wolf.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.170
<b>Work Diligently. Think Critically.
Strive for Excellence. Take Initiative.</b>

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.170
Midterm Exams

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:19.170
Begin.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:31.370
Well then...

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:34.060
Midterms

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.630
That's the first day done and dusted.

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:37.340
According to my own grading, 
at least I didn't do too badly.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.080
Still...

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.570
Japanese is one of his better subjects.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:47.350
If he were to get full marks, six points 
would be a significant gap.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:51.110
That's <i>assuming</i> he gets full marks, anyway.

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:55.020
And right now, I have no way of confirming.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:20.730
Why did you leave the last section blank?

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:27.900
There's no way you didn't know
 the answer to these questions, correct?

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.200
I didn't have time.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:36.760
I saw you stop writing ten 
minutes before time was up!

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:39.520
Do you think I'm stupid?!

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:42.090
You're holding back so I can 
get the top spot, aren't you?

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:45.900
Did you think that'd make me happy?
 Don't be ridiculous!

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:47.820
What was all that talk earlier?

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:50.760
Are you implying that I'd lose 
to you if you <i>didn't</i> hold back?!

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:52.300
Do you think I'm stupid?!

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.510
H-Hey... What's the matter, Yume?

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.950
Did you really think it'd be 
heroic of you to let me win?!

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:00.000
You're just belittling my intellect!

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.580
Like I can't win on my own!

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:04.460
I don't want a victory that's handed to me!

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:05.790
Stop!

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:08.150
Calm down, Yume! What's going on?

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:09.900
What gives?

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:11.280
Huh?

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:14.120
Getting the top spot is 
important to you, isn't it?

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.220
You said so yourself.

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:17.790
So I left some of them blank.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.410
What's wrong with that?

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:22.120
Oh no. Not you too, Mizuto-kun...

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:23.750
Mine-kun!

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:27.070
It doesn't matter to me 
if I come out on top or not.

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:31.260
Like you said, I couldn't care less 
about what anyone thinks of me.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:33.640
So I let you have it! Is that so wrong?!

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.080
It's not wrong.

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:41.380
It's just not right.

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:46.500
This isn't... who you are.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:53.910
Midterms

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:56.030
<i>Forget it.</i>

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:59.370
<i>Our rivalry was all in my head after all.</i>

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.860
<i>It's pointless to dwell on.</i>

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:03.790
<i>Why complain when I have one less 
person to contend with anyway?</i>

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:07.070
<i>If I'm to keep my new life as Irido Yume,</i>

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:08.870
<i>that top spot is my only concern.</i>

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:15.430
You have no right to define who I am.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:21.110
No one has the right to 
define that for you either.

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.340
Say goodbye, dear little sister...

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.190
to your precious life as a model student.

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:33.840
I think you meant <i>big</i> sister, 
my dear little brother.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:37.200
<b>Work Diligently. Think Critically.
Strive for Excellence. Take Initiative.</b>

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:37.200
Midterm Exams

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.700
Midterms

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:48.210
Midterms

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:55.090
Midterm Results

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:03.480
<b>Midterm Exams
Top 50 Students</b>

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.120
<i>It'll be fine.</i>

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:07.780
<i>I'm certain I scored above 90
 in every subject.</i>

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:11.480
<i>There's no way I </i>didn't<i> get first place.</i>

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:14.490
<b>Tanihara

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:17.610
<b>Asuhain

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:20.530
<b>Irido</b>

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:20.530
<b>Irido</b>

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:25.290
<b>Irido\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hMizuto</b>

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:25.290
<b>Irido\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hYume</b>

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:28.480
Fire Hydrant

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:28.830
Hey, Miss Second Place.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.730
I trust you're doing well.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:35.510
Those questions you skipped on the Japanese 
test were weighted pretty heavily.

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:40.580
You would've had to study a 
lot to overcome that handicap.

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:43.810
Going to such lengths... that isn't...

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:45.930
It isn't who I am, you mean?

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:48.440
Didn't I tell you?

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:51.880
I wanted a little taste of 
what it's like to be on top.

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:54.560
But I envy you.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:57.700
Getting second place seems like 
way less of a burden to bear.

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:04.200
Well, if you ever want your throne back, 
there's always finals, Miss Model Student.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:06.310
<i>"Miss Model Student"?</i>

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:10.330
<b>Irido\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hMizuto

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:13.340
<i>Oh, that's right...</i>

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:22.540
<i>I'm not the top of the class anymore.</i>

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:23.830
Yume-chan!

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.980
What an amazing one-two 
finish from the sibling duo!

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.040
You were so close, Irido-san!

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:32.400
I guess everyone meets 
their match at some point.

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:36.080
I bet those two'll be neck 
and neck for finals too.

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:38.170
<i>This wasn't the reaction 
I was expecting at all.</i>

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:39.690
No doubt. They're basically 
rivals at this point.

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:40.540
<i>Not getting the top spot...</i>

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:41.790
No way, I think...

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:42.410
<i>Failing...</i>

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:44.410
<i>What was I was so scared of again?</i>

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:46.370
What's wrong, Yume-chan?

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:48.710
<i>Now I see.</i>

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:50.890
<i>Nothing's changed at all.</i>

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:55.720
<i>The way they treat me, the way they 
look at me... It's the same.</i>

00:10:56.510 --> 00:11:01.050
<i>All this time, I thought being at the top 
of our year was what defined who I am.</i>

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:02.100
<i>But it never did.</i>

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.350
What is it, Yume-chan?

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:07.370
It's okay, it's okay!

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:09.260
Second place is still super cool.

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:12.400
What Maki said! Cheer up, Irido-chan.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.730
No, don't worry...

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:16.800
These are happy tears.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:18.570
Thanks so much, you guys.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:24.490
<i>Who else could do it but you?</i>

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:26.830
<i>I'm awkward and ineloquent...</i>

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:30.200
<i>An introvert in disguise, desperate 
to fool the world into thinking otherwise...</i>

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:35.640
<i>And you're the only weirdo out there
 warped enough to understand me!</i>

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:39.970
<i>When you do things like this, how...</i>

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:44.470
<i>Just how on earth do you expect 
me to live without you?</i>

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:45.970
<b>Library</b>

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:47.470
Wednesday, June 1st

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:51.730
<i>He's usually around here somewhere.</i>

00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:54.860
<i>There he is!</i>

00:11:57.590 --> 00:11:58.510
Oh?

00:11:58.510 --> 00:12:01.360
So you like that series too?

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.780
KonoSuba: God's Blessing on This Wonderful World!

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:09.700
<i>Huh?</i>

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:13.000
<b>My Stepmom's Daughter Is My Ex</b>

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.000
Wednesday, June 1st

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:20.510
Haganai: I Don't Have Many Friends

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:23.500
So, Higashira...

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:25.260
Y-Yes?

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.760
What might you define as a friend?

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.260
Haganai: 
I Don't Have
 Many Friends

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:30.560
Say no more.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:34.900
For this is one of the few topics 
I, Higashira Isana, am an expert in.

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:38.960
I've never seen someone so 
eager to define a word before.

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:40.900
This is definitely a first.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:44.610
I mean, just think about it.

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:47.710
It all depends on where you 
set the friend bar.

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:52.220
Consider my classmate on day duty who made
 sure I turned in my homework this morning.

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:55.120
I could call them a friend 
if I set the bar there.

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:58.420
Stop being arbitrary with the friend bar.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:01.880
Conversely, say someone I'm 
close to is getting bullied.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:07.100
I could say, "Oh, we're not that close,"
and take the heat off myself!

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:09.430
Revolutionary, isn't it?!

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:12.810
I don't think someone like you will 
be making friends any time soon.

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:16.850
But I consider you a friend, Mizuto-kun.

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:21.940
If you ever get bullied, 
I promise to get bullied alongside you.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:25.400
You wouldn't help? You're so unreliable.

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:27.420
Aw, I wouldn't go that far.

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:28.910
That wasn't a compliment.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:34.010
Guess it's time to head home.

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:34.910
Yup.

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.810
Now then, Mizuto-kun...

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:39.920
Could you put my socks on for me?

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.290
This again?

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:43.000
Don't be shy.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:45.800
<i>Higashira Isana is a friend of mine.</i>

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:47.300
<i>That said,</i>

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:52.910
<i>she's the first person I've ever clicked 
with this much in my entire life.</i>

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:58.300
<i>I could also live the rest of my life and 
never make a closer friend than her.</i>

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:02.400
Hiya!

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:05.240
So you're headed out now too, Irido-kun?

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:07.070
Yeah, guess so.

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:09.490
I-It's a real-life extrovert, Mizuto-kun!

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:11.870
<i>Did she just call him "Mizuto-kun"?!</i>

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:14.080
Who's that there beside you?

00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:15.830
Higashira Isana.

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:18.580
We met recently and hit it off.

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:21.720
I'm Minami Akatsuki!

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:23.840
I'm in the same class as Mizuto-kun.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:24.840
Nice to meet you!

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:31.850
She's a little shy, so just try 
to give her some space, okay?

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:35.360
It's rare to see you being 
so protective of someone.

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:37.430
Have you already introduced
 her to Yume-chan?

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:39.260
No, not yet.

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:40.760
Wait, what?

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:47.530
Wait up, Yume-chan!

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:51.720
Who's this "Yume" person?

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:53.960
My little sister.

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:55.040
Your sister?

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:56.540
Stepsister, actually.

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:57.910
Stepsister?!

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:01.580
Why'd you react more to the "step" part?

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.010
<i>Why do I feel so uneasy?</i>

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:10.500
<i>Could I be jealous?</i>

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:13.430
<i>I'm not even his girlfriend anymore.</i>

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:15.110
<i>And besides...</i>

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:19.450
<i>Siblings don't get jealous!</i>

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.940
Irido

00:15:27.490 --> 00:15:28.190
Here.

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:30.700
You want soy sauce, don't you?

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:32.460
Y-Yeah...

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:39.250
That's my eraser.

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:41.210
My bad.

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:44.580
That's okay. It's my fault for dropping it.

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:48.840
School Motto

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:48.840
<b>Work Diligently. Think Critically.
Strive for Excellence. Take Initiative.</b>

00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:51.340
Damn, I forgot it.

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:53.010
Here you go.

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:53.940
Huh?

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:59.020
You left your lunch at home, 
so I brought it for you.

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:06.770
My stepsister's acting strange.

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:09.900
Strange? How do you mean?

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:12.200
She seems distant.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.390
No...

00:16:13.390 --> 00:16:15.910
More like, I don't get annoyed 
when we talk anymore.

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:17.910
Isn't that a good thing?

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:20.120
It is, but it isn't.

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:24.870
Why don't you just go and ask her yourself?

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:28.130
It's a thought.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:31.090
You're quite the imbecile, Mizuto-kun.

00:16:31.640 --> 00:16:34.000
If you ask me, you should trust your gut.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:36.090
I'm sure you'll do the right thing.

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:39.260
Trust my gut?

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:40.540
U-Uh, scratch that!

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:44.230
I'm probably the least qualified 
person to be giving advice...

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:46.040
No, please continue.

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:49.730
I'll hear you out and decide
 for myself whether I listen.

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:59.240
Each and every person has their 
own set of criteria, right?

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:00.650
Criteria?

00:17:02.570 --> 00:17:08.240
An ideal model for how they 
want their life to be or to go.

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:14.220
When I feel that threatened, 
I get all... up in arms, you know?

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:18.010
People say I'm bad at going
 with the flow, and that's why.

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:21.140
That's it! The flow!

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:24.890
I've just been going with the flow around her.

00:17:25.180 --> 00:17:26.120
Huh?

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:27.450
Thanks, Higashira.

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:30.020
Talking to you really helped.

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:31.730
S-Sure...

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:34.990
Also, it's important to know
 how to go with with flow,

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:37.270
but you don't have to do that around me.

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:40.630
It'll be faster for me to just go with yours.

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:44.910
Th-Thanks for that.

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:50.440
<i>This feels great.</i>

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:54.520
<i>Who would've thought just forgetting 
about him would make life so much easier?</i>

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:04.650
Huh?

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:06.220
Wha...

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:09.050
What?!

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:14.070
Wh-What do you want?

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:18.780
Huh? What's this? What gives?

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:26.260
Wh-Wh-What are you—

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:31.790
The average human heart 
beats once per second.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:35.920
Yours, on the other hand, 
is clearly beating twice that fast.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:39.850
Does the sight of your mere stepbrother

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:42.880
wearing a different outfit than usual

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:46.560
really warrant your heart racing so, 
dear little sister?

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:50.020
N-No fair!

00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:54.820
So, why are you here?

00:18:55.180 --> 00:18:57.820
I dislike the way you've been acting.

00:18:57.820 --> 00:18:58.890
Huh?

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:03.320
The unreasonably calm, sincere, 
and understanding attitude.

00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:06.500
Talking to you lately doesn't 
irritate me in the slightest.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:08.960
Nary a sarcastic or snide remark.

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:11.830
You act like picking fights is beneath you.

00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:14.380
It's infuriating on all accounts.

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:18.900
If something's changed for you,
 I want to hear about it.

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:21.130
We're siblings, aren't we?

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:30.020
Listen, Onii-chan...

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.980
What's up, Little Sis?

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:37.110
I think I'm jealous of that girl.

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:39.470
That girl?

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:41.490
You mean Higashira Isana?

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:47.080
Until the very end, I always 
called you by your family name.

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:50.020
But she's already calling you "Mizuto."

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:54.360
The more I thought about it, 
the less I liked it.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:59.860
But we're siblings, so I don't 
have a reason to be jealous.

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:01.590
So that's why...

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.010
I get it.

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:10.140
Hey, can I ask you something?

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:11.640
What is it?

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:17.750
What bothered you so much about
 me not being snide or sarcastic?

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:22.400
I don't know.

00:20:22.810 --> 00:20:27.130
I didn't like you acting like what we 
went through never happened, I guess.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:31.980
<i>The relationship I so badly wanted to forget...</i>

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:36.570
<i>was the one relationship I would 
truly regret forsaking.</i>

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:45.130
<i>You've always been able to articulate 
what I could never put into words.</i>

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:51.640
So, Onii-chan... do you think it's 
okay to get jealous over a sibling?

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:52.840
No way.

00:20:52.840 --> 00:20:56.020
Getting jealous of your big brother's 
friend is just plain creepy.

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.230
Hey!

00:20:57.230 --> 00:20:59.180
But don't worry.

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:02.990
I've known you were a 
creep for over two years.

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:06.450
You're the creep, Onii-chan.

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:10.410
Hey, now you sound like a real little sister.

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:19.080
Thanks for always hanging 
out with Mizuto here.

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:21.740
I'm his older stepsister, Irido Yume.

00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:23.670
Nice to meet you.

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:25.530
<i>"Mizuto," she says.</i>

00:21:25.530 --> 00:21:27.390
<i>Skipping the honorific to one-up her?</i>

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:29.550
<i>Not to mention that smile...</i>

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:32.410
<i>You're gonna scare Higashira right 
back into her shell, you know?</i>

00:21:33.260 --> 00:21:36.860
Yeah, r-right back at you.

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:40.080
Wait...

00:21:40.080 --> 00:21:43.240
D-Did I do something weird?

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:44.680
Hey...

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:48.960
Just what kind of relationship 
do you have with Irido-kun?

00:21:48.960 --> 00:21:49.530
Huh?

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:51.910
W-We're just friends with similar interests.

00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:55.540
Oh... I didn't realize.

00:21:55.540 --> 00:22:00.290
U-Um, am I missing something here?

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:03.290
Well, you see...

00:22:03.290 --> 00:22:04.500
My sister...

00:22:05.450 --> 00:22:08.930
was under the impression 
that you had feelings for me.

00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:10.930
H-Huh?!

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:13.140
Hey! Why'd you have to tell her?!

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:15.020
I'm just telling the truth.

00:22:15.840 --> 00:22:17.140
He's ruthless.

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:18.700
Mizuto-kun.

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:25.660
This is the second time in my life 
that I've wished I was born a boy.

00:22:25.660 --> 00:22:28.440
The first time was when I got my period.

00:22:28.440 --> 00:22:31.660
I yearn for a body that doesn't 
bleed from the nether regions.

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:36.280
You're hearing this, right?

00:22:36.280 --> 00:22:39.960
You really think a girl would talk 
like that to the guy she liked?

00:22:48.220 --> 00:22:51.680
That said, they sure seem 
to get along, don't they?

00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:55.850
And I was all set to help her out 
if she was interested in him...

00:22:55.850 --> 00:22:56.970
You too, right?

00:22:56.970 --> 00:23:00.590
Of course. Assuming 
she <i>was</i> interested, that is.

00:23:01.840 --> 00:23:04.480
Well, Mizuto-kun, I'm going this way.

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:07.710
Okay. See you tomorrow, then.

00:23:07.710 --> 00:23:09.050
Right!

00:23:09.050 --> 00:23:11.740
A-A-And a-also...

00:23:13.530 --> 00:23:16.440
F-Farewell to you too!

00:23:18.880 --> 00:23:20.290
You did great.

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:28.520
So, Yume-chan...

00:23:29.670 --> 00:23:31.710
About what you just said...

00:23:31.710 --> 00:23:35.140
You're still game to help 
Higashira-san out, right?

00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:36.010
Huh?
